 "text": " What if the Eiffel Tower was made of human bones? The real tower is 7,300 tons of iron. Bone is about four times lighter. So if you built the same shape from bone, it would weigh about 1,800 tons. That's about 250,000 skeletons. Where would Paris get them? Right under its streets. The catacombs hold the bones of 6 million people. That's enough for 24 towers. So, would it stand? Pound for pound, bone is nearly as strong as the tower's iron, but it's much bendier, so it would sway in the wind, and the rain would slowly rot it away. Subscribe for more What Ifs.",
